{#
  Sonos event callbacks from the `restricted` segment to Home Assistant (ADR-082).

  Rendered by configure-ex50.yml (tag `sonos-callbacks`) and piped into the DAL
  Admin CLI like config.dal.j2. Unlike that from-factory delta, this one is
  safe to re-apply on the live box:

  - Static leases are list elements, so each is added only when its MAC is
    absent from the pre-apply `show config` (ex50_before). `add ... end`
    moves the CLI into the new element, so its fields are set relatively and
    each lease gets its own `config ... save` session (`save` commits and
    leaves config mode; the next `config` starts back at the root).
  - `firewall custom` leaves are scalars; re-assigning them is a no-op.

  `firewall filter` matches zones only (no address or port), so the narrow
  allow is a `firewall custom` rule. DAL runs the `rules` string through the
  shell whenever the firewall is rebuilt, after its own ruleset. That ruleset
  is legacy iptables with a single FORWARD chain: RELATED,ESTABLISHED accept
  first, then the zone accepts, then a final LOGDROP. So an `-I FORWARD` accept
  for new connections lands ahead of the drop, and replies ride the conntrack
  accept. The sets are flushed and refilled on every run so they always match
  network.yml; the iptables rule is inserted only if not already present.
  `override` stays false — true would replace DAL's whole firewall.
#}
{%- set nodes = [dell_inspiron_ip, intel_nuc_ip, optiplex_ip, quanta_ip] -%}
{%- set match = "-p tcp --dport " ~ sonos_event_port ~ " -m set --match-set ha-sonos-src src -m set --match-set ha-sonos-dst dst -j ACCEPT" -%}
{%- set cmds = ["ipset -exist create ha-sonos-src hash:ip", "ipset flush ha-sonos-src"]
      + (ex50_restricted_sonos | map(attribute='ip') | map('regex_replace', '^', 'ipset add ha-sonos-src ') | list)
      + ["ipset -exist create ha-sonos-dst hash:ip", "ipset flush ha-sonos-dst"]
      + (nodes | map('regex_replace', '^', 'ipset add ha-sonos-dst ') | list)
      + ["iptables -C FORWARD " ~ match ~ " || iptables -I FORWARD " ~ match] -%}
{% for s in ex50_restricted_sonos if s.mac | lower not in ex50_before.stdout | lower %}
config
add network interface restricted ipv4 dhcp_server advanced static_lease end
mac {{ s.mac }}
ip {{ s.ip }}
name {{ s.name }}
save
{% endfor %}
config
firewall custom override false
firewall custom rules "{{ cmds | join('; ') }}"
firewall custom enable true
save
exit
